WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
A journalist and advertising writer sets
out to write a sceptical book about Jesus'

2
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.550
last days.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.330
He says the evidence
led him the other way.

4
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.990
His book, published in
1930, asks a blunt question:

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.850
who moved the stone?

6
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.830
Decades later, Ian Wilson, a historian
by training known for work on the Turin

7
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.640
Shroud, takes up the same puzzle.

8
00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.160
What did these two investigators find?

9
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.580
And can history really
settle a question like this?

10
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.120
In this mission, you'll weigh
the rival explanations they test,

11
00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.520
from theft to a wrong tomb.

12
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.880
Then you'll compare their methods, with
the strengths and weaknesses of each.

13
00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.410
Your mission: find out what
the two investigators found,

14
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.240
and whether their method can work.
